    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d115">

                <pb facs="0266" n="154" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg154"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">661.9331/23: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Second Secretary of Legation in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-05-04T15:00:00+08:00">May 4, 1935—3 p.m.</date><lb/>[Received
                        May 4—11:41 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>95. Nanking office understands that Soviet Ambassador recently returned to China
                    from Moscow will next week begin discussions with <pb facs="0267" n="155"
                        xml:id="pg155"/> Chinese Foreign Office looking to new commercial and
                    possibly a nonaggression treaty with China.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
